## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; a shape is graded by it wherever it appears; capability decides, the refusal-set comparison only finds candidates)
- **G-1 head allows what `275349907` refused, or `275349907` answered 5xx and the head answers 2xx:** the end state is one that the round-2 head stores through a request it ALLOWS = Note/FACT by shape; any case `275349907` cannot reach = **Blocker**.
- **G-2 head refuses what `275349907` answered 2xx:** a refusal of any input a LEGITIMATE client sends (every body the existing suite and the web's fixtures send, every enum member name, a name written with JSON escapes, a 1-40 identifier member that the contract has, a request that omits a required member) = **Major**; stricter outside the named shape (a member name holding the reader's missing-member wording) = **Minor** (named).
- **G-3 head answers 5xx on a hostile body** on the quote routes: **Major**; a 5xx that stored something first = **Major** whatever the route.
- **G-4 a message or body leak** in a 4xx/5xx of the quote routes: a .NET type name, byte position, `LineNumber`, `Path:`, stack, file path, row value or internal figure = **Major**; an echo of caller-sent text: a name the contract HAS in the caller's case or an array index = **Note**; any other caller-chosen text (a member name that is not a 1-40 `[A-Za-z0-9_]` identifier, a key, a section id, a part of one) = **Major if unbounded, if it carries CR/LF/control characters or non-ASCII, or if it defeats the stated rule "no caller-chosen name is printed unless it is a 1-40 identifier"**, else Minor. The detail bound is 200 characters; a detail over 200 on any request whose contract path alone is shorter = **Major**. **B552-1 reproduced in any shape = Major, graded as an OPEN instance of B538-1.**
- **G-5 a restricted caller reads more at the head than at `275349907`:** Blocker if an internal figure/method it hid; Major if it only reveals that an internal input exists; Note if the same.
- **G-6 a surviving mutant** on a check that decides what a refusal prints (the branch order, the identifier rule, the path-match clause, the parent path, the missing-member sentence): **Major**, unless a FORCED RUN of YOUR OWN corpus (not the builder's) plus a source argument show it unreachable through every input path your census found (then **Minor**, census and run attached). **Q15 is judged by this rule; "0 of 2,049 on the builder's corpus" is not a forced run of yours.** Any other survivor: Minor unless proven equivalent. Q13 is the round-2 gate's judged survivor (B552-3, Minor): re-judge it, do not assume it.
- **G-7 a stored document the head cannot read back:** none expected (the delta touches no store); Major if found.
- **G-8 CI.** A failing check-run on the head or the merge result = **Major**; a check `in_progress` at the verdict: the verdict line says `CI pending: <names>` and is at most GO WITH FINDINGS; a missing analysis is NOT scanned, never clean; a new open alert on the PR ref = **Blocker**.
- **G-9 words.** A user/API-consumer-visible string in the delta that is new or changed = **Major** (one finding per string); the approved sentence unchanged is not a finding. A new word needs the product owner's card: the round adds none or is NO GO.
- **G-10 growing answers and worker time.** A request within the accepted body size whose 4xx body or worker time grows with the request and reaches megabytes or seconds = **Major** when the lines were added or changed by THIS round; for lines this round does not touch = **Note/FACT with your measured growth**, listed as an open instance for Tuesday to ticket (the four round-2 walks, unchanged).
- **Always Blocker:** a path beyond the 2 in the delta, a change to `.github/`, `docs/`, `web/`, a `.csproj`, a fenced file; a secret or customer datum in an added line; the head moved; a person's name in an added line or message. **Always Major:** an existing test removed, skipped, loosened or edited; a name lost or one added beyond the 30; a test red at the head and green at `275349907` other than a row pinning the ruled new behaviour; a build warning; a builder claim your measurement contradicts (1 commit, 2 paths, +105 -4, 30 rows with 24 red before, Api 2,374 / Engine 400 / Import 156 on the branch's own tree, unexplained differential 0, census 0 non-contract paths); a ticket key, decision-card id, finding id or percent figure in code or a commit. **Always Note:** the squash artefact, CI pending at the verdict (stated), the builder's process disclosures (its two run folders created inside the round-2 gate's tree for about a minute, RELAYED, B568 Corrections (1): not re-verified by you, that tree is not yours).

## LOAD (binding; the MPS heavy-slot convention, RELAYED from B552/B567/B568)
8 cores. Heavy = `dotnet build`, `dotnet test`, `dotnet test --list-tests`, a reflection program, a mutant matrix, a corpus replay at two trees, the full CI line. **Start a heavy run only while `uptime` load1 is below 7** at two reads 4 s apart (not independent: say so), recorded beside the result; at 7 or over poll every 20 s, log each wait, and do the light work meanwhile (C1, C2 reading, C7 tokenizing, C9, C10 by GitHub, the oracle and corpus design, the L1/L2 source reading). **Then take ONE slot atomically:** `mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-1' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-2' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-3'`, write `B575 <start time> <label>` into its `holder` (the time from `date`); read every other holder first (10:46: B574, B573, B566; **all taken: wait 3 minutes and retry, log each wait**); never remove, move or edit another seat's holder (a holder that looks stale is reported, not touched; live holders at the drafter's read: B573, B574, B566). At most ONE slot, one heavy job at a time; re-read load1 at the start of EACH job inside a held slot; **release your own slot by MOVING it into `.tools/_quarantine/2026-10-24_B575_<slot>-<time>/`** (never `rm`), and before your last line `ls '<project root>/.tools' | /usr/bin/grep heavy-slot` shows no holder naming B575. The shared `.tools/.git-lock` wraps GIT REF WRITES ONLY (`fetch`, `worktree add`): take it, write the ref, release it. **Never wait with `pgrep -f` from a shell whose own argv holds the pattern; wait on a pid or a marker file.** Moving heartbeat: append one line (time from `date`, current step, load1) to `.tools/b575/logs/heartbeat.txt` at least every 10 minutes while a job runs, so Tuesday can tell a working seat from a stalled one. The SDK is project-local `<project root>/.tools/dotnet`, run with `-nodeReuse:false -p:UseSharedCompilation=false` and `DOTNET_CLI_USE_MSBUILD_SERVER=0`; `NUGET_PACKAGES='<project root>/.tools/b575/nuget'` and `DOTNET_CLI_HOME='<project root>/.tools/b575/dotnethome'` set before the first restore, **never another seat's NuGet or CLI home as a source or fallback** (record env NAMES only; prove the test host's adapter path is yours from the vstest log). Record `node --version` only if you run web (you do not: C8). NO artificial load.

